-- title:
--   A polynomial bound for the local Gaussian moment remainder
-- statement:
--   Write \(a_n=\log n/\log\log n\) and \(L_C(n)=\lceil Ca_n\rceil_+\),
--   where \(\lceil x\rceil_+=\max\{0,\lceil x\rceil\}\). For \(d\ge0\) and \(S,b\ge0\), put
--   \(T_n=S+\sqrt d\,\sqrt{2(b+4)\log n}\) and \(A_n=T_nS+S^2/2\). Let \(C>0\) and define
--   \[
--   \rho_n=\frac{2e^{2A_n}A_n^{L_C(n)+1}}{(L_C(n)+1)!}.
--   \]
--   For all sufficiently large integers \(n\),
--   \[
--   \rho_n\le2n^{1-C/8}.
--   \]
